`InferenceIncidLogBinomial.Rd`: proposed example NOT applied, it does not pass the check (default part under 4 s, CPU/elapsed at most 2.5, every seed clean): with \donttest, seed 2 of 5: warning: InferenceIncidLogBinomial: dropped covariate(s) x1 and refit because the fit with all covariates failed or did not pass the fit checks (e.g. no convergence or no usable standard error). The reported results are for the reduced model. Suppress with suppressWarnings(expr, classes = "edi_covariate_dropped_warning").. Cause given: With only 10 subjects, a covariate and a 50% event rate, the log-binomial MLE hits the exp(Xb)=1 boundary or the covariate fit fails, so warnings are raised.

```r
seq_des = DesignSeqOneByOneBernoulli$new(n = 60, response_type = 'incidence')
for (i in 1:60) {
  seq_des$add_one_subject_to_experiment_and_assign(data.frame(x1 = rnorm(1)))
}
seq_des$add_all_subject_responses(rbinom(60, 1, 0.2))
\donttest{
inf = InferenceIncidLogBinomial$new(seq_des)
inf$compute_estimate()
}
```
